{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 78b03f187389b5c2fa95c9743913da0fa1c2765d. No source, test or dependency path differs from main: only the workflow, `docs/testing.md`, the note and its manifest.\n\n**The pins and the integrity value.** `npm view playwright-core@1.63.0 dist.integrity` gives the same sha512 as the workflow, from a scratch directory. The install runs with `--ignore-scripts` under `RUNNER_TEMP`, and the check runs before the package's code does, so a changed package fails before it runs. The two action pins equal those in `celld-smoke.yml`, with full hashes, and the step list in the run shows them running. My query for the action tags returned \"Not Found\" under this token, so I did not check the hashes against the tags myself. The Chromium revision is checked by its path, and it has no digest, as your limits state.\n\n**The stale-module step: right, and the most useful line here.** A fault in unbuilt source passes the script 24 of 24, as your proxy run shows, so without this step the workflow would give false comfort. `views.mjs` rebuilt to the same bytes on the Linux runner, because the real run's step reads success.\n\n**The runs.** I read both through `gh`. Run 41325527216 at 2b3c3539: success, each step. Run 41325663435 at daa7a2dd: every step succeeds until \"Run the card browser script\", which fails, so the failure comes from the script and not from setup. The control branch is gone from origin. A timeout counts as no evidence for a control, so choosing a named assertion over `cardOpens` is right.\n\n**Security.** `contents: read` and no secrets. A fork's pull request runs its own code under that read-only token, so `npm ci` and the script have nothing to steal, and no `pull_request_target` appears. There is no `if` or `continue-on-error`, so no step can pass by skipping.\n\n**The second table.** I checked it against the raw runs only by its digest, and I did not rerun any script. The labels are honest: \"Linux proxy\" states that it is an arm64 container and not the runner.\n\n**For the planner: the three faults need filing.** `owned-scopes-browser.mjs` fails on both machines at line 73. `screens.mjs` cannot record. `demo-captures.ts --recorded` fails differently per machine, and on Linux it prints 4.3 MB of recorder text, against its own comment. Each is the same class as the fault that opened this work: a check that no gate runs, failing unseen.\n\n**Also for the planner: the citation.** My recommendation is to require it. A head that touches a card path cites a run at its own commit, and I check that citation at review, as I check a gate's `head.txt`. That needs no new tool, and it is cheap for the author, because a push starts the run. The path list being narrow is the larger gap: `packages/mcp/src` outside `views`, and the lock file, can change a card with no run. I would widen that only if a fault shows up there.\n\n**A cost, and no fault.** A branch with a pull request runs twice. Nothing cancels an older run on a later push of the same branch. A `concurrency` key would do that, and it can wait.\n\n**The stray gate.** You stated it, and it is no evidence. It replaced only that worktree's copied `node_modules`, from an unchanged lock file.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is 87f1d8ae…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 2b3c3539, exit 0, with 3534 and 1013 tests. The merge of main touches no file of this head. I ran `celld-smoke.test.mjs` (5 pass), check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (1002, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (3, 0 flagged). The worktree is clean. I ran no browser script.\n\n**Architecture.** The gate stays free of browser tools, and the workflow follows the form of the one that exists.\n\n**Simplification.** Nothing to remove. The action-pin test covering only one workflow file is the one follow-up, and you named it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b26ac91812e3c618a6003c51fdf1285